{
  "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80e1-b497-e99561eae658",
  "title": "Spring Boot starters",
  "sourceUrl": "https://xpandeyed.notion.site/20824eb1ed5480e1b497e99561eae658",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-0",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Starters"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-0-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A Spring Boot starter groups libraries for one Spring feature under one dependency."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-0-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "spring-boot-starter-web",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " supplies Spring MVC and JSON support for the servlet web examples."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-0-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It also brings in an embedded Tomcat server in Spring Boot 3.5."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-0-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A starter changes the project\u2019s dependencies. It does not generate application classes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-0-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Adding a starter and starting its feature are separate steps. The auto-configuration lesson explains how Boot configures the added libraries."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-0-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Declare Spring Web in Maven",
        "language": "text",
        "description": [
          "The complete `pom.xml` includes the Spring Web starter and Boot dependency management.",
          "`DemoApplication.java` is the application startup class.",
          "The project requires Java 17 or later and Maven."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "The starter supplies the web libraries through their declared dependencies.",
          "The dependency has no individual `version` because Boot dependency management supplies it."
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Dependency management"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-1-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot\u2019s dependency management selects library versions intended to work together for that Boot release."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-1-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The generated Maven project normally inherits it through "
        ],
        [
          "spring-boot-starter-parent",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-1-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The generated Gradle project supplies equivalent dependency management through its configured plugins or platform."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-1-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A version override changes the combination selected by Boot. It needs a compatibility reason."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-1-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A starter does not necessarily supply every external dependency. For example, a database still needs its driver."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter-projects-auto-configuration-lesson-1-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Later lessons name their required starter before using its classes."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  "updatedOn": "2026-10-20",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Official reference: Spring Boot starters",
      "url": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/3.5/reference/using/build-systems.html"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Add Spring features through starters and keep Boot-managed library versions."
}
